## Attribution

This is the digital twin of the instrument cluster for
**TVSRideCompanion** (https://github.com/athulkrishna2015/TVSRideCompanion),
and reuses material from it under the same non-commercial terms:

- **TVSRideCompanion** — https://github.com/athulkrishna2015/TVSRideCompanion
  Licensed **CC BY-NC 4.0**. The wire format in `ntorq/protocol.py`, the
  maneuver table in `ntorq/pictograms.py`, and the frame layouts throughout
  are the mirror image of that project's protocol package: where that code
  builds the frames the *phone* sends, this builds the frames the *cluster*
  sends and parses the phone's. The two must agree byte for byte.

- **overclock98/JupiterRideCompanion** — https://github.com/overclock98/JupiterRideCompanion
  Licensed **CC BY-NC 4.0**. The navigation control and text packet layouts,
  and the maneuver byte table, originate there.

- **TVS Motor Company** — the Ntorq 125 owner manual. Display element
  positions, gauge bar counts, litre thresholds, the display modes and every
  alpha-numeric message reproduced in `ntorq/cluster.py` and `ntorq/display.py`
  come from it. It is cited per fact rather than paraphrased.

Protocol constants and byte layouts were independently transcribed from the
`com.tvsm.connect` application (v8.14.1); the official application is not
redistributed here.

"TVS", "SmartXonnect" and "Ntorq" are trademarks of TVS Motor Company. This is
an unofficial, unaffiliated interoperability project.
